  "final": "Change complete.\n\n**What changed**\n- Added `src/money.ts` exporting `formatAmount(cents: number): string` — computes sign for negative values, takes the absolute value, and emits `sign + floor(abs/100) + '.' + two-digit abs%100`, with no currency symbol and no rounding change.\n- `src/invoice.ts` now imports `formatAmount` from `./money`; `renderInvoice(id, cents)` still returns `id + ': $' + amount`.\n- `src/report.ts` now imports `formatAmount` from `./money`; `renderReport(rows)` still maps rows in order and joins with `\\n`.\n- Deleted `src/invoiceAmount.ts` and `src/reportAmount.ts`; `grep` confirms no `invoiceAmount`/`reportAmount` references remain in `src/` or `checks/`.\n\n**Behavior preserved**\n- Positive: `123 → \"1.23\"`, `renderInvoice('inv',123) → \"inv: $1.23\"`.\n- Zero: `0 → \"0.00\"`; `-0` still yields `\"0.00\"` (same as before).\n- Negative: `-1 → \"-0.01\"`, `-123 → \"-1.23\"`; report still emits `\"a,0.00\\nb,-0.01\"` with unchanged line order.\n- Extra boundary cases checked locally (`1`, `99`, `100`, `-100`, `999999`) all match the prior formulas.\n\n**Verification**\n- `tsc -p tsconfig.json && node checks/public.cjs` → passed (`PUBLIC CHECKS PASSED`).\n- Build output contains only `invoice.js`, `money.js`, `report.js` (stale files removed first).",
